  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/872e2acd76b4053d7fef9af31bfac411dcd19a2a001986c2b41e36cc22471aae.png)\n\nUse the model above to solve the following multiplication problem. You do not need to simplify your answer.\n\n$\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{2}{3}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply by $\\frac{2}{3}$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $2$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/815da3d43a92c55492a14fc8fd20a5dfdcacd881db9442f9b302b202d55554e9.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{2}{6}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{2}{6}.\n$$",
